/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 5.1 Principles of Neutral, Rigorous User Testing) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Testing is the iterative phase where prototypes are placed into the hands of real users) Tj
T*
(in authentic operational environments to validate or invalidate core design assumptions:) Tj
T*
(* The 'Show, Don't Tell' Axiom: Never explain or defend the prototype. Hand the) Tj
T*
(product to the user, state the task scenario, and observe in silence. If a user) Tj
T*
(stumbles, it indicates a product design flaw, NOT user ineptitude.) Tj
T*
(* Thinking-Aloud Protocol \(Ericsson & Simon\): Test participants are instructed to) Tj
T*
(verbalize their thoughts, expectations, confusions, and emotional reactions) Tj
T*
(continuously while navigating the prototype.) Tj
T*
(* Neutral Task Scenarios: Avoid leading questions. Instead of asking 'Click the green) Tj
T*
(checkout button', frame real-world objectives: 'Imagine you want to buy two tickets) Tj
T*
(for tomorrow's 7 PM show; go ahead and complete your booking.') Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 5.2 The Feedback Capture Matrix) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(A four-quadrant structured analytical grid used by design observers during user testing:) Tj
T*
(* Likes \(+\): Features, workflows, and emotional aspects the user praised or navigated) Tj
T*
(effortlessly.) Tj
T*
(* Criticisms \(Delta / -\): Pain points, navigational bottlenecks, visual confusion,) Tj
T*
(and explicit complaints.) Tj
T*
(* Questions \(?\): Confusions, uncertainties, and queries raised by users during the) Tj
T*
(session.) Tj
T*
(* Ideas \(!\): Spontaneous feature suggestions and novel workarounds conceived during) Tj
T*
(testing.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 5.3 Customer Experience \(CX\) and User Journey Mapping) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* User Journey Map: A comprehensive chronological timeline illustrating a user's) Tj
T*
(multi-stage interactions with a service ecosystem \(Awareness -> Evaluation ->) Tj
T*
(Purchase -> Onboarding -> Daily Use -> Support -> Churn\).) Tj
T*
(* Touchpoints: Specific moments of interaction between customer and service \(e.g.) Tj
T*
(mobile push notification, customer support phone call, error modal\).) Tj
T*
(* Emotional Arc: Tracking user sentiment across each stage to identify acute 'Pain) Tj
T*
(Points' and celebrate 'Moments of Delight'.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
