T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 5.4 Usability Heuristics and Universal Accessibility) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(* Jakob Nielsen's 10 Usability Heuristics for UI Design:) Tj
T*
(- 1. Visibility of system status \(appropriate real-time feedback within reasonable) Tj
T*
(time\).) Tj
T*
(- 2. Match between system and the real world \(familiar user language, concepts, and) Tj
T*
(metaphors\).) Tj
T*
(- 3. User control and freedom \(clear emergency exits, undo, and redo actions\).) Tj
T*
(- 4. Consistency and standards \(platform conventions; words mean the same across) Tj
T*
(screens\).) Tj
T*
(- 5. Error prevention \(proactive design preventing errors before they occur\).) Tj
T*
(- 6. Recognition rather than recall \(minimize user memory load; visible options\).) Tj
T*
(- 7. Flexibility and efficiency of use \(keyboard shortcuts and accelerators for) Tj
T*
(experts\).) Tj
T*
(- 8. Aesthetic and minimalist design \(no irrelevant or rarely needed information\).) Tj
T*
(- 9. Help users recognize, diagnose, and recover from errors \(plain language error) Tj
T*
(messages\).) Tj
T*
(- 10. Help and documentation \(concise, searchable, task-oriented help\).) Tj
T*
(* Universal Accessibility \(WCAG 2.1\): Pour Principles \(Perceivable, Operable,) Tj
T*
(Understandable, Robust\) ensuring usability for individuals with visual, auditory,) Tj
T*
(cognitive, and motor impairments.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
([CASE STUDY 1: Nielsen Usability Audit on E-Commerce Checkout]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: An e-commerce platform experienced a 68% shopping cart abandonment rate) Tj
T*
(on its final checkout page.) Tj
T*
(Heuristic Evaluation Findings:) Tj
T*
(- Violation of Heuristic #1 \(Visibility of System Status\): When users clicked 'Pay Now',) Tj
T*
(the screen froze for 4 seconds without a spinner or progress bar. Anxious users clicked) Tj
T*
(repeatedly, resulting in double-billing.) Tj
T*
(- Violation of Heuristic #3 \(User Control & Freedom\): If a user made a typo in their) Tj
T*
(shipping address, the back button cleared their entire credit card details.) Tj
T*
(- Violation of Heuristic #5 \(Error Prevention\): Allowed users to enter credit card) Tj
T*
(numbers without automatic spacing or format validation.) Tj
T*
(Design Interventions: Implemented real-time field validation, sticky cart summaries,) Tj
T*
(visual progress indicators, and one-click address editing.) Tj
T*
(Measurable Results: Shopping cart abandonment dropped from 68% to 27%, generating $3.4M) Tj
T*
(in incremental revenue.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
